Article 6 Resource tax shall be exempted under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Crude oil and natural gas used for heating during the extraction of crude oil and the transportation of crude oil within the oilfield;
(2) Coalbed gas extracted by coal mining enterprises for safety production needs.
Resource tax shall be reduced under any of the following circumstances:
(1) A 20% reduction of resource tax on crude oil and natural gas extracted from low-yield oil and gas fields;
(2) A 30% reduction of resource tax on high-sulfur natural gas, tertiary oil recovery, and crude oil and natural gas extracted from deep-water oil and gas fields;
(3) A 40% reduction of resource tax on heavy oil and high pour-point oil;
(4) A 30% reduction of resource tax on mineral products extracted from mines in decline.
Based on the needs of national economic and social development, the State Council may prescribe exemptions or reductions of resource tax for circumstances conducive to promoting resource conservation and intensive utilization and environmental protection, and shall report such prescriptions to the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress for recordation.
